# Trivia Quiz

An interactive and scalable **Trivia Quiz web application** built using **HTML, CSS, and JavaScript**.

This project started as a learning exercise inspired by a quiz concept seen in the **Mimo learning platform**, but has evolved into a more structured and feature-rich application focused on:

- application architecture
- UI state management
- scalable styling systems
- maintainable project structure

The quiz demonstrates how to build a modern browser application **without frameworks**, while still applying professional structuring techniques.

---

# Live Demo

View the live project here:

https://blackravenwolf.github.io/trivia-quiz/

---

# Purpose

This project exists as a **practical web development learning project**.

Main learning goals:

1. Strengthening JavaScript fundamentals
2. Building interactive UI applications
3. Understanding scalable CSS architecture
4. Managing application state
5. Structuring maintainable frontend projects
6. Improving UI/UX and visual hierarchy
7. Learning debugging workflows

---

# Features

The quiz currently includes:

### Core Gameplay

- Large structured question database
- Questions divided into **difficulty levels**
  - Easy
  - Medium
  - Hard
  - Expert
- Random question selection per quiz round
- No duplicate questions within one session
- Randomized answer order (shuffle logic)
- Multiple choice answers using radio inputs
- Validation: user must select an answer

### Quiz Flow

- **Start Screen**
- **Options Screen**
- **Credits Screen**
- **Quiz Screen**
- Restart quiz with a new random question set
- Return to main menu

### Quiz Settings

- Select difficulty level
- Select number of questions (Quick / Standard)
- Select multiple quiz categories
- Live preview of current settings

### Feedback & Progress

- Real-time score tracking
- Question progress indicator
- Animated score progress bar
- **Countdown timer per question**
- Timer progress bar animation
- Correct / incorrect feedback states
- Final quiz completion state

### UI / UX

- Glassmorphism styled quiz card
- Gradient overlay background image
- Window-style header bar
- Centered responsive layout
- Smooth visual feedback
- Desktop / Tablet / Mobile responsive breakpoints

### Code Architecture

- Quiz data separated from logic
- Modular CSS architecture
- Structured project folders
- Maintainable component-based styling
- DOM state driven UI rendering

